10/30/2026 v1.2.8: Update RAJA (v2026.07.1), CHAI (v2026.07.1), Umpire (v2026.07.2), BLT (v0.7.2), Caliper (2.15.0), and added Adiak (0.5.0).
- Added explicit Umpire memory management alongside optional CHAI support, including immediate GPU allocation and initialization, and field copies.
- Added automatic device-pool sizing based on problem dimensions and decomposition, a --dev_pool_size override, and reporting of pool size and memory high watermark.
- Added GPU-aware MPI, and optional direct Umpire allocations for communication planes.
- Added asynchronous CUDA/HIP sweep execution and processing of all ready subdomains during sweep scheduling.
- Corrected GPU kernel loop ordering, including the LTimes GDZ case, field-copy direction, and host/device synchronization and transfers.
- Expanded Caliper instrumentation to cover main() and solver iterations. Added Adiak metadata for configuration, problem size, performance, and device-pool usage.
- Adopted C++20, reorganized CMake into a superbuild (to accomodate Adiak), improved bundled/external profiling-library integration, and added CUDA 13 compatibility.
- Added H100 CUDA configurations for GCC and Clang, MI300A and Intel 2024 configurations, and updated existing ROCm and compiler configurations.
- Added Hubcast configuration.

10/31/2023 v1.2.7: Update RAJA (v2023.06.1), CHAI, Umpire (v2023.06.0), and BLT (v0.5.3). Updated use of RAJA GPU threading API. Added host-configs for new platforms/compilers, and scripts to aid release process.

05/26/2022 v1.2.6: HIP fixes.

04/26/2022 v1.2.5: Update RAJA, CHAI (v2022.03.0), Umpire (v2022.03.1), and BLT (v0.5.1). Added HIP support.

07/14/2019 v1.2.4: Updated to BSD-3-Clause license, Caliper support

10/12/2018 v1.2.3: CUDA support, updated policy selection/dispatch mechanisms, updated build system

04/04/2018 v1.2.2-CORAL2: Fixed bug in Population edit

03/26/2018 v1.2.1-CORAL2: Updated to RAJA-0.6.0rc2, fixed FOM calculation and updated docs

11/02/2017 v1.2.0-CORAL2: Initial release for CORAL2

